{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then a small deterministic specification that encodes exploration, one-shot recovery, and directional obstacle handling. The spec favors random_walk in clear space, inserts a short move_forward pulse after clear exploration for coverage, uses move_backward only as a brief front-obstacle escape, and returns to exploration as soon as path_clear is observed. Action states self-loop on path_clear so uncontrollables do not preempt the intended pulse in the same step, while obstacle events can still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate unrestricted sensing and actuation plants from the policy specification.",
    "Use a small number of policy states: clear exploration, short forward progress, front recovery, left recovery, right recovery, and a rare blocked-scan fallback.",
    "Ensure every obstacle-triggered state enables exactly one safe controllable and never enables move_forward or random_walk.",
    "Bias toward coverage by alternating random_walk in clear space with a short move_forward pulse, and by returning directly to exploration on path_clear after recovery."
  ],
